- **F11-2** [note] `crates/c3/src/panel/run.rs:2412` - After a re-seat, patch_routing_picked warns when sessions.json cannot be read, and it still ignores a failed to_bytes or write_text_atomic, so routing.picked can stay at the build-time draw with no line. Trigger: A re-seat has rewritten the in-memory sessions and write_text_atomic returns Err, or to_bytes fails. Evidence: read-code: A read Err or missing file prints could not rewrite routing.picked and returns.; read-code: The write is let _ = write_text_atomic inside if let Ok(bytes) = sessions.to_bytes(), with no else. Verify: Force write_text_atomic to fail after a re-seat fixture and confirm stdout has no routing warning while sessions.json still lists the lost member. Remedy: Print the same one-line warning when to_bytes or the atomic write fails.

